# IANA backzone (almanac-sourced), Sierra Leone (Freetown) -- one hour BEHIND GMT (-1:00)
# from 1 Jul 1913, with a 20-minute seasonal shift to -0:40 (Sep-Mar, 1932-1939), then GMT
# from 6 Dec 1941; vs default link to Africa/Abidjan (GMT), which is a full hour fast across
# the 1913-1941 standard periods (and 40 min fast in the -0:40 seasons).
#
# NOT Shanks-sourced: Shanks's International Atlas prints Sierra Leone with a 0:40 seasonal
# save (Jun-Oct) and a GMT switch in 1957 -- both CONTRADICTED by IANA's almanac-sourced
# rules (a 0:20 save, and the wartime GMT switch on 6 Dec 1941). Shanks is DEFERRED (the
# sourced-primary-beats-Shanks discipline, as with Bahrain / Indochina); SL_1 reproduces
# backzone Africa/Freetown exactly (696/696 vs backzone, mid-months 1912-1969).
# A dated transition list re-expressed as a zic source (the reference tzdata
# compiler input). Cross-check: IANA:Africa/Freetown (backzone).
# Rebuild the compiled TZif with:  rake shanks:build
